    "terrainName": "berlin",
    "description": "What: on berlin two identical STOCHASTIC platoons (30 men, defending), 7 km apart. A PHYSICAL 'Red Squad Forced' (four armed men) stands 250 m from the first - inside C-7's forced range (300 m); a 'Red Squad Planned' stands 450 m from the second - inside the band, outside the forced range. Judge: (1) the first platoon hands over at once, skipping the planning time (its Planning stage is never seen), before any stochastic step fights it (no stochastic fire line, no slot hurt); (2) the control platoon goes through Planning first, then hands over; (3) CE-8307: the forced platoon splits ONE level at a time but all at once - its 3 squads and their men are created held and hand over in the SAME tick as the platoon, so no squad ever fights stochastically in contact. Fail: a stochastic step on the forced one, the forced one planning, or a squad handed over stochastic. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh agg-forced-handover"
  },
